# Tests

`node:test` + `node:assert/strict`, no test framework packages. Run with `npm test`; type-check with
`npm run check` (tests are type-checked too).

| File | Covers |
| --- | --- |
| `test/unit.test.ts` | pure functions and small modules (parsers, settings, versions, device list) |
| `test/server.test.ts` | the real server via `startServer()` from `test/helpers.ts`: API, static files, index.html ids |
| `test/checks.test.ts` | library checks: DAT parsing, CRCs, duplicates |
| `test/browser.test.ts` | headless Chrome over CDP: every section at desktop and phone width; skipped without Chrome |

## Rules

- Tests never touch the real workspace, `.cache/`, the network or a handheld. Use temp folders:
  `fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "manager-..."))` and remove them in `t.after()`.
- Code that reads `ctx` paths: save and restore with `setRoot()` and `ctx.cacheDir` in `t.after()`.
- Server tests use `startServer({ GB: ["Tetris (World).gb"] })`; it boots `src/main.ts` on a free port with a
  throwaway workspace and cache. Call `srv.api(route, body?)`.
- Name tests as a sentence describing behaviour: `test("trash refuses empty or unsafe requests without touching files", ...)`.
- A new dialog or view adds its element ids to the list in `test/server.test.ts`.
- A bug fix adds a test that failed before the fix when practical.
- Run one file or test: `node --test test/unit.test.ts --test-name-pattern "workspace"`.

For manual checks in a browser (temp server, fake TF2 card, cleanup) use the `manager-testing` skill.
